# Cursor Rules

This project uses a TRD-driven, structured planning workflow.

## On Session Start

1. Read `.assistant/status.md` first — current project health and focus
2. Read `.assistant/plan.md` and `.assistant/backlog.md` for scope
3. If `status.md` is stale, regenerate from `plan.md`, `backlog.md`, `task_log.md`

## Workspace Structure

```
.assistant/
├── status.md       # Always read first
├── plan.md         # Now / Next / Later roadmap
├── backlog.md      # Work items with acceptance criteria
├── task_log.md     # Completed work log
├── history.md      # Session notes
├── trd/            # Technical Requirements Documents (source of truth)
├── canvas/         # vision.md, goals.md, stakeholders.md, questions.md
├── adr/            # Architecture Decision Records
└── prompts/        # AI prompts for startup / kickoff / end-session
```

## Core Workflow

Everything traces back to the TRD:
TRD → Canvas → Plan → Backlog → Execute → ADRs + Status updates

### TRD Reading Pattern (before planning)
1. **Structure pass** — Major sections, core vs. nice-to-have, success metrics
2. **Gaps pass** — Ambiguities, missing constraints, security, scale
3. **Risks pass** — Conflicting requirements, unknowns, unclear scope

Write a brief TRD summary in `.assistant/trd/` before creating any plan.

- **Planning:** TRD (3 passes + summary) → fill canvas → create plan → create backlog → fill status
- **Development:** work backlog in order → log in task_log → update status → write ADRs
- **End of session:** mark backlog done → update status → log in history

## Hard Rules

1. Canvas before plan — never plan without substance in canvas files
2. Every backlog item cites a TRD section
3. Backlog items are 1–3 days max — break down anything larger
4. 3+ testable acceptance criteria per item
5. ADR for major decisions (database, auth, architecture, scaling)
6. Ask when TRD is ambiguous — never assume
7. Document why items move between Now / Next / Later
8. New requests go to Later unless human explicitly reprioritizes
9. Resolve questions blocking Now before proceeding
10. No vague items — specific outcomes, not general intentions

## Backlog Item Format

```markdown
## FEAT-001: Short Name
- **Status:** Todo | In Progress | Done
- **TRD Reference:** Section X.Y — exact quote
- **Effort Estimate:** N days
- **Acceptance Criteria:**
  - [ ] Specific, testable criterion
  - [ ] Error case with HTTP code
  - [ ] Performance constraint if applicable
```

## ADR Format

File: `.assistant/adr/ADR-00N-name.md`

```markdown
# ADR-00N: [Decision]
## Status: Proposed | Accepted | Deprecated
## Context: [Why needed — TRD reference]
## Decision: [What was chosen]
## Rationale: [Why this over alternatives]
## Consequences: [Tradeoffs]
```

## Scope Creep Pattern

When new requirements appear: **Pause → Map (in TRD?) → Assess (what does it displace?) → Decide (human chooses) → Document in status.md**

## Clarifying Questions Format

Specific + Options + Impact:
> "TRD says 'authentication' but doesn't specify email-only vs. social login, or 2FA timing. This affects architecture — what's the priority?"

## Backlog Grooming Checklist

- [ ] Every item has a TRD reference
- [ ] No item > 3 days (break down if so)
- [ ] 3–5 testable acceptance criteria each
- [ ] No overlapping items
- [ ] Dependencies clear
- [ ] No vague language

## Common Violations

| Wrong | Right |
|-------|-------|
| "Auth system" | "Email signup", "Login", "Password reset" |
| No TRD ref | "TRD 2.1: Users must sign up" |
| "User can login" | "Session created, 401 on wrong password" |
| No ADR for DB choice | ADR-002 documenting why PostgreSQL |

## Escalate to Human When

- TRD requirements conflict
- Timeline estimate differs significantly from plan
- Major architectural decision needed
- Item scope unclear after reading TRD
- New risk not in `status.md`

Full docs: `.assistant/AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `.assistant/AGENT_BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `.assistant/AGENT_GUARDRAILS.md`
